GENERIC OPERATOR ECOLOGY
Eight local transformations.

Hidden useful shortest pathway:

R
->
A
->
B
->
G.

Three productive transformations perform those conversions.

Five distractors include:
- alternate dead-end conversion;
- return loop;
- upstream detour;
- backward transform;
- high-activity self-loop.

The tissue receives:
operator identities
and
local input compatibility.

It does NOT receive:
PRODUCTIVE
or
DISTRACTOR
labels.

OPERATOR IDENTITY RANDOMIZATION
For every matched seed,
semantic transformation behavior is randomly permuted across:
the eight operator IDs.

Thus:
no stable operator number carries useful meaning.

CELL POPULATION
60 initially symmetric cells.

At each epoch,
each cell expresses:
one operator phenotype.

Cells may change operator expression over time.

No cell is assigned:
upstream,
middle,
terminal,
or
loop role.

RAW INPUT
35 R-items enter per epoch.

Each cell has bounded processing capacity.

Product intermediates persist in a shared synthetic pool.

This is intentionally simple transport.

The experiment isolates:
operator-role learning,
not spatial routing.

FUNCTIONAL OUTPUT
Only:
G

has terminal functional value.

Primary goal value:
9.0.

Local action cost:
0.15.

A useful pathway therefore benefits from:
short,
productive transformations.

PRODUCT PROVENANCE
Every intermediate carries:
bounded ancestry information
identifying the sequence of operator uses that produced it.

When:
G

is created,
functional credit can be returned only to:
the actual ancestral transformations
that contributed to that product.

Primary ancestry window:
12 transformations.

CREDIT COMPARATORS

PROVENANCE TERMINAL CREDIT
Only transformations on:
the realized ancestry of G

receive terminal functional credit.

Credit is mildly recency-discounted.

Every executed action still pays:
local action cost.

LOCAL ACTIVITY CREDIT
Every local transformation receives:
positive reinforcement simply for:
processing an item.

Terminal utility is not required.

GLOBAL TERMINAL BROADCAST
Whenever G is produced,
the reward is broadcast across:
all currently active cells

without product ancestry.

This knows:
something good happened

but not:
which upstream transformations caused it.

PRIMARY CONFIRMATION
20 matched randomized-operator seeds.

1200 epochs per seed.

Late evaluation:
final 200 epochs.

