PRIMARY GLOBAL-CREDIT NEGATIVE
A global terminal reward tells the tissue:

SOMETHING WE DID WORKED.

But it does not identify:

WHICH TRANSFORMATIONS
WERE ACTUALLY ON THE PRODUCTIVE PATH.

The resulting role ecology remains:
noisy
and
under-specialized.

Provenance credit strongly outperforms:
global reward broadcast.

RANDOMIZED-IDENTITY RESULT
Because operator IDs are permuted independently each seed,
the productive role fractions cannot come from:
hardcoded operator number,
position,
or
initial preference.

The learned signal is:
functional ancestry.

EMERGENT DIVISION OF LABOR
No explicit rule says:

one-third upstream
one-third middle
one-third terminal.

Yet the mature population settles near:
17 / 19 / 21 cells

across the three productive transformations.

The terminal role receives slightly more population
because:
its input becomes the final bottleneck
under the tested processing geometry.

Thus:
role proportion can emerge from:
PRODUCT FLOW ECONOMICS.

This connects directly to:
H71 work ecology.

FALSE-INTERMEDIATE LOOP
Several distractor operators can create:
abundant local intermediates
or
recycle existing products.

The activity learner preferentially occupies those loops.

The provenance learner does not,
because:
activity that fails to enter successful terminal ancestry

does not receive:
functional credit.

PRIMARY CAUSAL PRINCIPLE
AN INTERMEDIATE SHOULD EARN CREDIT
BECAUSE:
IT WAS USED DOWNSTREAM TO PRODUCE FUNCTION,

not because:
it existed,
moved,
or
was repeatedly transformed.

This is the operator/pathway analogue of:
H59 consequence-gated vasculature.

